Z||000003||Phaeton||01-26-2000||12:42 AM||||All other things being equal, the Fiero gets better traction than just about any other rwd car.  But! performance tires have a harder rubber compound and do not stick to snow well. And wide tires combined with the Fiero's light front end tend to float the front and exagerate the understeer already there.  Living in alaska I invested in a set of 14 inch steel wheels and put 185/75 studded tires on them, better traction and steering than most fwd cars.  My grandmother left oklahoma in a covered wagon back in 1907, said we get more snow here in alaska, so spending that much money to make snow speeder may not be worth it.  ||||reg||1
